  "text": "## Projects Department Health &amp; Safety Standards\n\n## Ref:EGY/PRJCTS/HSE/REQs\n\n- Emaar Misr will advise of any additional specific KPl's and other data which they routinely require tobemeasured and reportedincludingbut not limited to:\n- Weekly HSE Flash Report:\n- ?Number of accidents, incidents and near misses reported in the week.\n- 0Number of hours worked (staff and labor) on the project.\n- Number of staff and laboremployed on theproject.\n- eAny achievements or concerns.\n- &gt;Monthly Health and Safety Report\n- tGeneral overview\n- Critical issues\n- eAccidents,incidents and near misses\n- ?Numbers and types of health and safety inspections and audits\n- o Numbers and types of Observations recorded and corresponding numbers of open/closed observationreports\n- Achievementsand accomplishments\n- GHealth and safety data and statistics\n\n## 2.4.3.1. Competency:\n\n- &gt;Having a wel-trained and competent workforce is essential if work is to be carried out safely and without harming those doing the work or those others who may be affected by the work.\n- At every level within the Program Partners organization and within those of their suppliers and subcontractors site personnel, supervisors, managers, auditors, advisers, general operatives and others shall be competent to carry out their particular duties and tasks, or be adequately supervised if under training. It is the responsibility of the Program Partners to:\n- Ensure both specific task competence and also core health and safety competence for construction workthrough their organization and theirsuppliers\n- ·To make use of suitable competency schemes where available\n- To maintain and promptly provide on request adequate records such that competence may be readily demonstrated\n- &gt; Supervisors and managers shall have practical and documented access to competent advice on health and safety matters\n\nAamr Mler FoA\n\nTaxard218-287-209\n\nDuvuiopnelnt SA.E\n\nCR12841\n\nCetru, Lar\n\n